:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F5=Refresh
:PD.Shows the display again with the current information.
:PT.F10=Display detailed messages
:PD.Display detailed messages.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F16=Job menu
:PD.Job menu.
:PT.F17=Top
:PD.Moves to the top of the list.
:PT.F18=Bottom
:PD.Moves to the bottom of the list.
:PT.F24=More keys
:PD.Shows the other function keys of the display.
:PT.F17=Top
:PD.Moves to the top of the list.
:PT.F18=Bottom
:PD.Moves to the bottom of the list.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/MSGLINE'.MSGLINE
:P.The MSGLINE of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/ALLKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F5=Refresh
:PD.Shows the display again with the current information.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F16=Job menu
:PD.Job menu.
:PT.F17=Top
:PD.Moves to the top of the list.
:PT.F18=Bottom
:PD.Moves to the bottom of the list.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/STKKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F5=Refresh
:PD.Shows the display again with the current information.
:PT.F11=Display activation group
:PD.Display activation group.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F16=Job menu
:PD.Job menu.
:PT.F17=Top
:PD.Moves to the top of the list.
:PT.F18=Bottom
:PD.Moves to the bottom of the list.
:PT.F22=Display entire field
:PD.Display entire field.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/THREAD'.Thread
:P.The thread shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/RQSLVL'.Type
:P.The type of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/PGM'.Program
:P.The program of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/PGMLIB'.PGMLIB
:P.The PGMLIB of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/STMT'.Statement
:P.The statement of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/PROC'.Procedure
:P.The procedure of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/LIBLKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F16=Job menu
:PD.Job menu.
:PT.F17=Top
:PD.Moves to the top of the list.
:PT.F18=Bottom
:PD.Moves to the bottom of the list.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='LIBL/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/LIB'.Library
:P.The library of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/LIBTYPE'.Type
:P.The type of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/ASPDEV'.ASP device
:P.The ASP device of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/LIBTEXT'.Text
:P.The text of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='LIBL/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.5=Display objects in library
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to display objects in
library it. The Display Library (DSPLIB) command runs for the entry.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/OPNFKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F5=Refresh
:PD.Shows the display again with the current information.
:PT.F11=Display I/O details
:PD.Display I/O details.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F16=Job menu
:PD.Job menu.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/ODPS'.Number of open data paths
:P.The number of open data paths shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/OFILE'.File
:P.The file, by name and library.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/OLIB'.Library
:P.The library of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/OMBR'.Member/ Device
:P.The member/ Device of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/OSCOPE'.Scope
:P.The scope of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/OACTGRP'.Activation Group
:P.The activation group the program runs in&colon. a named one, a new
one each call, or the caller's.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
